<title>BELGIUM: EU says lira rate in line with Italian economy.</title>
<headline>EU says lira rate in line with Italian economy.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said the central rate of the lira against the Ecu set by EU finance ministers on Sunday was in line with the Italian economy.  </p>
<p>The new central rate is 1906.48 lira per Ecu.</p>
<p>&quot;The chosen central rate of the lira against the Ecu is fully in line with Italy's economic performance and with market sentiment,&quot; Commission President Jacques Santer and Economic Affairs Commissioner Yves-Thibault de Silguy said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The consolidation of public finances under way, lower inflation and falling interest rates are factors for durable stability of the lira within the system,&quot; they said. &quot;The decision of the Italian authorities is a further sign of Italy's desire to achieve a high degree of durable convergence as soon as possible.&quot; - Brussels newsroom  322 287 6800</p>
</text>
